<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Thorpe returns one week after his first visit and is seen the same day by Dr. Ferrante of otolaryngology (head and neck surgery). The biopsy site on his lip has healed over. The pathology shows invasive, well-differentiated keratinizing squamous cell carcinoma. He started aspirin, atorvastatin and metoprolol a week ago and has had one episode of chest tightness walking up the hill to the ball field, which eased with rest; he did not need nitroglycerin. He had his echocardiogram this morning. He feels the metoprolol a little in his legs on the first days but less now. He asked many questions about the operation and how his lip will look and work afterwards, and whether he can keep coaching. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Biopsy</td><td>Invasive well-differentiated squamous cell carcinoma</td></tr><tr><td>Angina</td><td>One episode on a hill, eased by rest</td></tr><tr><td>New medicines</td><td>Aspirin, atorvastatin, metoprolol for one week; mild leg tiredness easing</td></tr><tr><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Done this morning</td></tr><tr><td>His questions</td><td>The operation, the look and function of his lip, and coaching</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
